{
  "id": "variable-stimulus",
  "term": "variable stimulus",
  "definition": "In psychophysics, a variable stimulus is a comparison stimulus that is presented alongside a standard stimulus and varied across different values along a sensory dimension such as loudness, roughness, or brightness. The observer judges whether this changing stimulus is greater, less, or equal to the standard.",
